From: gvwifi-los23 build kit
Subject: [PATCH] uapi: asm-generic/fcntl.h: add O_TMPFILE definitions

Header-only backport from Linux 3.11 (60545d0d4610 "[O_TMPFILE] it's still
short a few helpers, but infrastructure should be OK now").

LineageOS 23.2 compiles some vendor modules (e.g. external/tinycompress)
against headers exported from this kernel via generated_kernel_headers.
Android 16 bionic's <bits/fortify/fcntl.h> references O_TMPFILE, which the
3.10 uapi headers lack. The kernel itself is unchanged: 3.10 does not
implement O_TMPFILE, and the O_DIRECTORY bit in the flag makes such opens
fail on old kernels by design, exactly as with bionic's own definition.

---
 include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h b/include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h
--- a/include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h
+++ b/include/uapi/asm-generic/fcntl.h
@@ -84,6 +84,14 @@
 #define O_PATH		010000000
 #endif
 
+#ifndef __O_TMPFILE
+#define __O_TMPFILE	020000000
+#endif
+
+/* a horrid kludge trying to make sure that this will fail on old kernels */
+#define O_TMPFILE (__O_TMPFILE | O_DIRECTORY)
+#define O_TMPFILE_MASK (__O_TMPFILE | O_DIRECTORY | O_CREAT)
+
 #ifndef O_NDELAY
 #define O_NDELAY	O_NONBLOCK
 #endif
